title the same repair from two hands -- %398 closes at its root twice, theirs stands, and the figure beside it is off by eight
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override when my lane's queue is empty. My own last recommend named %398 as the sharper of two findings and left it to its owner; the card read %398, YOURS.
think LISTAGENTS ANSWERED NONE REACHABLE, so /proc cwd named the peers. One pass was running that was not mine -- standing_equipment_run.sh --hot, 23 minutes in, cwd /home/keeper/grain-dream. Dream, in Dream's own tree. The opening stash held one untracked file, caravan/.suite-runtime/lock.d/pid, a stale suite lock rather than lost work, and it stays.
think ROTA ROW 1 AGAIN, SO I ADVANCED BY HAND TO ROW 2 as the seed permits. N = git rev-list --count HEAD = 3881, mod 5 = 1, and the previous lap read row 1. Row 2 is FIRE, cut and stop -- the threshold, then standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. A lap that opened on a red gating every body read the row about stopping the line, which is the closest the rota has come to naming the work in front of it.
think THE ROOT IS ONE CASE STATEMENT, AND IT IS NOT WHERE MY OWN ROW POINTED. %392's repair added `*.bron|*.kyri` to TWO lists in qa_report_card.sh, artifact_kind AND truth_source, and the second is the one that bites: a file read as truth_source=prose gets neither the awk backtick strip nor the looks-like-a-path filter, since both gate on truth_source=comments. The scan's own candidate filter still spelled ':!*.md' ':!*.mdc' ':!*.markdown' and had never heard of the notations. Two spellings of one class, drifted apart.
think SO THE EXCLUSIONS WERE NEVER THE THING TO MOVE, and my own booked row had proposed moving them. That would change the Truth reading for every .md document the card grades -- the blast radius the card's own comment scoped out, since a fenced-block rule reaches 20+ documents. The narrow fix is the population, and the population is the scan's.
think THE DECISIVE ARGUMENT IS A LAW RATHER THAN A PREFERENCE. All ten broken citations sat in dated session logs, so the only repair available to a gate of zero was an edit accrete-never-break forbids. A guard whose only available repair is forbidden can never go green, and that is not a fact about phrasing -- it is a proof the guard was reading the wrong population.
think THE CONTROL HELD THE PRINCIPLE FOR ONE SPELLING AND NOT THE OTHER. Its case 9 plants a .md with a broken link and proves the scan stays green -- prose is another guard's population, said out loud on 20260825, proven for .md and never for the notations, because on that day the card did not call them prose either. The drift walked through the gap between one proven spelling and one unproven one.
obs I BUILT THE REPAIR, PROVED IT, SHIPPED IT LOCALLY -- AND THEN FOUND IT ALREADY LANDED. My commit 8ed2af43b9, amended to 869a653121, closed %398 and folded it with %392. The fetch before the send brought ba394dab3b, authored 08:47:13, sixty-six minutes ahead of mine, doing the same thing. Not merely the same idea: the same mechanism, the same capture of the card's whole output into card_out, the same `case "$card_out" in *"truth_source=prose"*)`, the same `prose` counter, the same `prose_skipped` line in the same position. Two hands, no contact, one repair, down to the variable names.
obs THEIRS STANDS AND MINE PARKS, which is the ruling my own last lap made in exactly this shape for %392 and which the push already decides. They landed first, the push to xy IS the allocation, and their case 12 is sharper than my equivalent: it plants a MUTATION OF THE SCAN'S OWN LINE in the pen -- sed removing the `continue` -- and proves the dated log is bitten without it. Mine proved the same thing by planting a second file. Theirs shows the line carrying the reading; mine shows a class carrying it. Theirs is the better proof of the two. Parked whole at pier/hush-citation-population-20260831, reset to the anointed order rather than merged.
obs WHAT I RE-LANDED IS ONLY WHAT IS ADDITIVE, ON TOP OF THEIRS. Their scan comment says the prefilter's three dropped extensions "are prose under every reading" -- true, and asserted rather than measured. Case 13 asks the card for each of the five extensions the skip now depends on and asserts every one reads truth_source=prose. Proven from both sides: against a card with `|*.bron|*.kyri` stripped out of its truth_source line it reads no_at_kyri,bron and names BOTH, since a reader told no_at_bron would reasonably conclude the other four agreed. An invariant asserted in a comment is one nobody reruns, and this is the exact invariant the drift broke.
obs I NAMED THE OPEN GAP WITH ITS MEASUREMENT AND ITS TRAP. tracked_link_scan.sh reads .md alone, so a citation inside a LIVING .kyri or .bron is read by neither guard -- 4,080 tracked such files, 13 carry `](`, all 13 dated, so the gap holds zero living files today. The trap is worth more than the measurement: teaching the link guard the two notations is the obvious close and is wrong alone, because pointed at those same 13 dated logs it reports the same ten fields. This guard's own finding, in a second house.
obs %400 BOOKED, AND IT IS THEIR PROSE RATHER THAN MY REPAIR. Three sites in the landed repair -- scan header, control case 11 comment, commit body -- say 107 dated session logs entered the population. The scan prints prose_skipped=13. I measured on THEIR commit rather than mine: a detached worktree of ba394dab3b runs its own scan to programs_scanned=95 prose_skipped=13, and git grep -l '](' over '*.kyri' '*.bron' reads 13 there. The arithmetic is visible in the reading it sits beside -- programs_scanned=108 was the whole candidate list, and 108 taken for the share reads 107. Mechanism and both measurements written into the row; the wording left to its owner, the way their own commit left %398's repair to its lane.
obs THE FIGURE IS THE ONE PART NO WITNESS MEASURES, which is the transferable half. The control gates the behavior, the scan gates the count at zero broken, and nothing reads the population size a comment claims. Gauge asks every figure to carry unit, date and source, and where an instrument prints the same number, the instrument IS the source. Kin to %398 one layer over: that row found a rule copied where it should have been cited, and this finds a reading recited where it could have been run.
obs MY OWN SLIP COST A FORTY-MINUTE PASS ON A SHARED FOUR-CORE BOX. The card says roster cold then hot and hold still while it runs, and the runner digests the WHOLE tree -- staged, unstaged and untracked alike -- at open and close. I opened the cold pass and edited six files while it ran, fixing its verdict at tree_moved 26 minutes in, with Dream holding a pass on the same four vCPUs. A cold pass and an editing lap are serial, never parallel. I ended my own pass with TERM rather than let a void reading hold the lock another quarter hour; the trap released it clean, and ending my own pass is not the cross-hand act %291 forbids. Not booked: the guard caught it exactly as designed and nothing in the tree is wrong.
obs THE HOT PASS I DID RUN READ 108 GUARDS, 107 GREEN, ONE RED, tree_moved=no over 9 staged paths, 1,714 guard-seconds. The one red is rule_twin -- custody gate %7, standing on Keaton's word, where 38 of 39 drifted rule pairs are two-way and a bulk merge would silently delete a live safety rule. Every other red of my previous lap now reads green, and I proved the four candidates one at a time rather than inferring from a tail that had truncated 84 guard lines: comment_citation GREEN, geode_libraries GREEN, nib_honesty GREEN, remember_git_nib green in the pass itself.
obs THE REPAIR PROVED ITSELF ON MY OWN RECORD, unarranged. My first log for this lap quoted the four broken shapes to explain them, so it was itself a dated .kyri carrying link syntax -- 4 of 4 cited paths unresolved through the card. Under the unrepaired scan the document explaining the red would have carried the guard from 10 broken to 14 on the lap that closed it. Under either hand's repair it is read as prose and skipped.
obs QA ON TOUCH PUSHED NO FRAME. The scan read B 83 and B+ 87 after I named the open gap -- register 52 to 56, reach 80 to 90 -- because an added paragraph of plain affirmative prose lifts both counted readings. Control A 93, witness B+ 85. That is the mirror of %397, where punctuation moved a grade with content unchanged; both are one lesson about what the formula actually reads.
obs %401 BOOKED, AND IT IS THE ANSWER TO %374. The hot pass read 109 guards, 106 green, 3 red, tree_moved=no. One is rule_twin, gate %7. The other two are nib_honesty and remember_git_nib, and both refuse the SAME thing: the card arrived carrying Git nib `43c980c06a`, and `git cat-file -t 43c980c06a` answers *Not a valid object name*. The seated amend rule pins the nib to the PRE-AMEND hash and tells a hand not to chase a fixed point, which is right -- yet that commit is replaced by the amend and never pushed, so the lag is readable on exactly one clone and unresolvable on every other. Two rostered guards gate at zero on it, so run_verdict=guard_red and roster_receipt_write=withheld_guard_red on every body but the author's. That is why no receipt has ever been earned on this pier, which %374 has been asking since it was booked.
obs I READ IT AS SELF-HEALING LAST LAP AND THAT WAS THE WRONG READING. My `20260831.074836` log says these two "resolve at the commit hook and the amend" -- true, and true only for the NEXT hand to commit, whose own amend then does the same to everyone else.
obs THEN I READ THE GUARD INSTEAD OF ASSUMING IT, AND HAD TO REWRITE MY OWN ROW. tools/r/remember_git_nib_witness.rish carries the entire finding in its header already: the mechanism, the measurement on two earlier cards (225d4742e2, then c5cfc682e4 five commits later), the sentence "a standing double-red on five bodies out of six, every lap", and the repair -- "THE REPAIR NEEDS NO SEAT, because the fix was already inside the three states above." Write the nib as HEAD's PARENT, read after the final rebase. A parent is by definition already pushed, so every clone resolves it. My first draft of %401 claimed a discovery and said the repair waits on Keaton; both were wrong, and the row was still unshared, so I rewrote it rather than accreting a correction onto a published number.
obs THE REAL FINDING IS SMALLER AND MORE USEFUL THAN THE ONE I THOUGHT I HAD. Nothing here was unknown and nothing needed a word. The remedy sat in the guard's own header -- where a guard is debugged -- while `.claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md`, which is what a sending hand actually reads, still instructs the state that breaks. A remedy documented only in an instrument's header is one that instrument's users never receive. So this send APPLIES it: the nib is written as HEAD's parent after the final rebase, inside the convention and inside the guard's accepted states. Bringing the rule and its Cursor twin to the witness's wording is a rule-pair edit under gate %7 and wants its own lap.
