recommend keep-going -- %398 IS CLOSED, BY A HAND THAT REACHED IT FIRST, AND I LEFT THEIRS STANDING. The whole lap is one finding worth more than either repair: two hands with no contact wrote the SAME mechanism down to the variable names, which says the shape was forced by the problem rather than chosen -- and it is also sixty-six minutes and two full roster passes spent twice on one line of shell. The fleet has no way to see that a red is being worked. A claim is written in a session log nobody reads until after they push, and the card's %398, YOURS said the opposite of what was true. WORTH YOUR WORD: whether an OPEN row gains a claim field -- seat and stamp, written when work starts rather than when it lands -- so the second hand reads it before spending the morning. MINE NEXT is %397's named remainder, shared machinery every body runs: a card that reads a reference block BESIDE the prose rather than inside it. Then spool_cloth's eight ClothError paths. YOUR GATES: %374's receipt chain, %5, %6, %7 -- rule_twin is the one red on the pier and it is yours. NAMED, NOT TAKEN: %400's three sites are their prose; the living .kyri/.bron citation gap is zero files today and its obvious close is a trap; my parked branch holds nothing theirs lacks except case 13, which I re-landed.
